WEBVTT

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.980
<b>800 years ago</b>

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.950
No!

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.330
Save me, Grandfather!

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.770
There's no need for tears, Rin.
 The demons are gone.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.070
That's not it, Grandfather!

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.880
I'm frustrated because I'm powerless 
and always need to be protected!

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.060
I just can't stand it!

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.570
Of all the things to cry over...

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:54.190
For now, let us protect you while 
you gain experience for yourself.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.700
That's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.820
But never forget...

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:05.110
We will be gone one day, 
and when new Idaten are born,

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.080
it will be you who must protect them.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:23.020
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.010
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:57.690
Now then, that about demonstrates 
the kind of strength we're dealing with.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.260
Impressions?

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:02.700
<b>#3
Whirlwind</b>

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.700
I was hoping they wouldn't 
be worth the consideration...

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.110
But they're potentially more dangerous 
than I initially thought.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.300
What gives, Piscalat-neechan?

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.750
Even I could beat those guys.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.670
Damn it, Cory, I told you 
not to bring fish in here!

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.680
That aside, I agree with him.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.380
Are we running around hiding in human form 
because we're scared of these worms?!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:26.020
It's asinine! We should get to work 
on demolishing the world straight away!

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.900
Hey, Neput, would you pipe down for a second?

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.440
Otherwise I'll kill you.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.960
R-Right, sorry.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.810
Now, I understand where both 
of you are coming from.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:40.610
Let me break this down for all of you.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:45.530
First, raise your hand if you 
think you can defeat these two.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.120
That's almost everyone.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.870
Now how about this brat?

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:59.350
Okay, suppose that there are several 
of them as strong as this boy here...

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.180
in addition to their master, 
who is orders of magnitude stronger?

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.740
Nickel and Brandy...

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.480
You two are likely the only ones
 up to the challenge.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.080
Umeyo, Miku, Barcode...

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.980
How do the current demon
and human populations fare numbers-wise?

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:25.360
There are currently 364 demons, with our 
human troops numbering 80 million.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.410
The general population stands at 220 million.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.210
The human population 
is growing nice and steady!

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.910
We've got all the potential 
laborers we could need.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.080
The real problem here is the demons.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.420
How are there only 364 after a hundred years?

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:45.210
You're young! Would it kill you 
to pump out a few yourself?

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:51.060
Well, this is all secondary. The main issue 
is we can no longer simply remain hidden.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.940
They are now aware of our existence.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.510
So should we strike immediately?

00:04:58.510 --> 00:04:59.690
Exactly!

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:05.320
Amidst my encounter and self-destruct, 
I placed a transmitter on the boy.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:06.970
A transmitter?

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:07.700
Yes.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.900
It was stuck to Hayato when he 
came back from chasing the doctor.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.770
The impact may have damaged it, however,

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.530
as the audio signal yielded dead air.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:21.460
Nevertheless, it pinged 
from the same location for a week

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.630
until its tracking signal also 
abruptly cut off the other day.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:29.690
I removed its audio hardware 
and discreetly placed it on Rin-san,

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:34.640
but I noticed it was gone the other day. 
And I'm sure the enemy has, as well.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.150
They'll dispatch someone 
to this location in short order.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:42.150
We have no way of knowing what other 
comrades they may have! As such...

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:46.150
we're going to play our strongest card.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:51.550
I'm positive that whoever they send 
will be able to defeat Hayato.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:56.380
Rin-san won't budge from the sealing ground.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:00.670
In other words, the enemy
 will have to deal with <i>her</i>.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.050
Ysley, Paula. It's time to train.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.200
R-Right!

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.970
Well, let's go...

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.220
Hey, wait, Ysley!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:15.070
Doesn't this mean we'll be forcing 
Rin-san to fight the enemy by herself?

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.230
What if she loses?

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:22.310
Has she, at any point in the last week, 
given you the impression that she'd lose?

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:25.510
Well, no, but...

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:31.110
Besides, Paula, if the enemy we're dealing 
with has the means to defeat Rin-san...

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:34.870
Then we never stood 
a chance in the first place.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.330
Therefore you'll be the one
 seeing to this matter,

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.780
Nickel.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:39.950
'Kay!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:44.710
You nasty, raggedy, dried up, 
nasty, dusty, crusty, old bat!

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.560
From underground?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.270
A little too predictable, Haya...

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.520
<i>Paula?</i>

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.570
Over here, Granny!

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.200
How's that, you damned fossil?

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:16.790
Well, that's the first hit someone's 
landed an attack on me in 200 years.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:26.570
Now, Ysley, are you all out of tricks?

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.560
Damn it all...

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.360
If I finally manage to hit her

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.970
but she doesn't even feel it, 
then I'm seriously out of my league...

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:46.270
Okay, I'm heading down!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.620
What's going on?

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:00.870
Only four of you in all? What a shame!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.480
<i>Wh-Who is this person?</i>

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:11.630
<i>A human? But this feeling...</i>

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.310
Oh, she ran!

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:15.550
<i>It's like a giant demon... in human form.</i>

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:17.890
Hey, who the hell are you?

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.810
From your outfit, I'm guessing 
you're with that old coot.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.930
What exactly does a human 
think they're doing—

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.640
That's one!

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.440
S-Son of a bitch...

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.810
What the hell was that for?!

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.780
Huh...

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.720
Oh, right, I forgot all about this!

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:40.790
That's not enough to kill you.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:45.750
I guess I get to experiment 
and see how much it takes!

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.720
Screw you!

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:04.460
Now, how much of a mess do I have to make 
of your insides for you to stay dead?

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:10.460
Hey, maybe this'll be easier than I thought.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:20.380
You're an odd one for a human.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:23.370
I'll be taking over from here.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.630
I see! You must be the leader.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.050
Hold up, Granny...

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.820
Mind your own damn business!

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:37.260
I'm gonna murder this—

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:43.740
Ysley, take Hayato and Paula and get clear.

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:44.680
Right.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.160
Damn...

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:54.210
Please be careful, Rin-san. 
That's no human. It's a demon!

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.320
What?

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:59.320
You should really pay attention!

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.540
With your arms extended so far out...

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.370
doesn't that make responding 
quickly more difficult?

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:22.770
<i>Sh-She's fast! Fighting at that distance 
is out of the question!</i>

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:23.510
<i>In that case...</i>

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:28.690
Gross.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:33.930
Get smashed!

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:55.060
I-I've had...

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.220
about enough!

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.850
But now you can't use your hands! 
Will your legs be enough to keep...

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.090
H-

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.900
Huh?!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.780
<i>How'd she recover already?!</i>

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.530
Remarkable!

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:28.040
A decent match for Rin-san?

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:31.290
Ysley, why are we stopping here?

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.410
Let's get farther away!

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:37.080
No. We have to stay 
where Rin-san's can see us.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:40.050
Any farther away is dangerous.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:47.020
<i>Four-eyes has got a good 
head on his shoulders.</i>

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:50.510
<i>If I take a pot shot at this range 
and they peg my position,</i>

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>they'll flee.</i>

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:56.190
<i>Never thought I'd see anyone put up 
a decent fight against Nickel, though...</i>

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:22.970
So having your neck skewered 
doesn't kill you, either...

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.890
I'm kinda getting sick of this, seriously!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:28.780
I guess this is why Pi-chan was 
worried about fighting you guys.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.770
Hold on. I have one question.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.560
Just what are you, exactly?

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:44.940
I'm not entirely sure what you're asking...

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:49.000
But I'm a demon. Do I look 
like a human or something?

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.200
Indeed you do.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:56.320
I saw all manner of demons 800 years ago,

00:12:56.320 --> 00:13:00.510
but none of them were intelligent 
enough to communicate,

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:03.620
and there were certainly none who looked

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.150
<i>as human as you do.</i>

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:12.970
<i>So, normally, demons have the appearance 
and intelligence of that monster we saw?</i>

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:16.010
<i>That must mean the doctor is...</i>

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:21.530
We were granted human intelligence and forms!

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.450
Surely even you've heard of him, yeah?

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:28.320
Our great Demon Lord and leader,
 His Amazingness, Over-M!

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.370
I thought as much. Did he pick "Over-M" 
because it vaguely sounds like "Obami"?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:35.650
And did he really need to throw in
 the "Demon Lord" title?

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:38.410
There's a palpable lack of thought 
in his naming choices.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.670
Wait, when did you put 
the transmitter on her?

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.690
Earlier.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:45.120
More importantly, I think I understand 
a bit more about who we're dealing with.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.190
I'd wager he's actually a mere human.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.660
A Demon Lord? I doubt it.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:53.870
He probably just implanted false memories 
to make the demons easier to control.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:57.440
Which is why, if I'm right, the 
next thing Rin-san says will be...

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.890
Who is that?

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:00.670
Never heard of him.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:10.120
Well, the specifics may elude me,
 but you're not human, right?

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:15.950
And if you're just a demon, 
I'll eliminate you right now.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.420
<i>She pulled a sword from her hand?</i>

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:22.340
<i>There's just too much here that I don't get!</i>

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:27.000
<i>A human-made sword shouldn't 
even put a scratch on Nickel...</i>

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.840
<i>But that thing might be bad news!</i>

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:33.820
Huh?! What is that?! 
Where'd she get that sword from?!

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:36.250
It's like my glasses and clothes.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.430
You can change your own clothing 
at will, can't you, Paula?

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:39.170
Yeah.

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:42.080
Still, weaponry would have to be

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.980
a fundamental part of your lifestyle...

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.720
in order to conjure up something like that.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.240
I'd like to see you eliminate me, lady!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:58.250
<i>I said that, but she's bound 
to lop off a few of my arms.</i>

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:01.270
<i>It's a sacrifice I'll have to make.</i>

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:06.730
<i>And in exchange, I'll attack with 
my full strength using my tail.</i>

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:13.800
<i>After that, I won't give you 
a chance to regenerate!</i>

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:17.810
I'll tear you to shreds in an instant!

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:30.530
It seems you and your so-called Demon Lord
 doesn't know a thing about us Idaten.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:34.570
You thought one of you would be enough?

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:39.360
Because I've never seen 
any demon capable of defeating

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.540
a fully-trained Idaten solo.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:44.040
<i>Wh-What...?</i>

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:47.460
<i>I can't move...</i>

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:51.320
It's over, Ysley, Paula. You can come back.

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:58.470
What is this?

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.600
Some sort of paralysis or sealing technique?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:06.740
Induced paralysis? Grandfather 
did have a technique like that...

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:08.360
It's beyond me, though.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.780
Don't screw with me! Then what did you do?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.860
Why can't I move my body?!

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.320
That's only natural...

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:22.000
Your head's not connected to it.

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:30.820
<i>Eight hundred years ago,
the demon threat was eliminated,</i>

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:32.720
<i>ushering in a long age of peace.</i>

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:37.480
<i>In that peaceful world, 
Rin was the last remaining Idaten.</i>

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:42.510
<i>Yet her heart was consumed 
by overwhelming fear...</i>

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.590
<i>I'm scared! I'm scared! I'm scared!</i>

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:50.300
<i>Why? What is there to fear? 
Grandfather's seal is perfect!</i>

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:52.210
<i>The demons should be gone for good!</i>

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:55.880
<i>But what if it's broken? 
What if there are surviving demons?</i>

00:16:55.880 --> 00:17:00.460
<i>Grandfather and the others are gone!
 There's no one left to protect me!</i>

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:02.650
<i>I'm all alone...</i>

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:05.120
<i>And I'm defenseless!</i>

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:13.510
<i>For a long time after that, 
Rin spent her days cowering in fear.</i>

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.970
<i>As flora spread and fauna populated,</i>

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:21.890
<i>she finally came to realize
 that the demons were truly gone.</i>

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.930
<i>Thus she began to take action.</i>

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.810
<i>This was fifty years after the sealing.</i>

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:31.230
<i>What Rin sought in the peaceful age...</i>

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:32.690
<i>was power.</i>

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:36.700
<i>Overwhelming combat ability.</i>

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.660
<i>She had no idea exactly how strong 
she would need to become,</i>

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.650
<i>but over the course of 350 years,</i>

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:45.840
<i>she thoroughly tempered her body 
as if to purge her fears,</i>

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.620
<i>growing ever stronger.</i>

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:52.690
<i>In another 200 years' time, 
Rin was entirely free of fear.</i>

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:57.090
<i>When Prontea, the first Idaten
 born in the age of peace,</i>

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.140
<i>completed his training under her...</i>

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:03.810
<i>That was the day Rin finally felt at peace.</i>

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.540
<i>And for the first time in 
six centuries, she smiled.</i>

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:16.690
Wh-What?

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.540
I-Impossible!

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.200
<i>What is it, G-Thirteen?</i>

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:24.120
How's the battle shaping up? 
Is Nickel struggling?

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:24.700
<i>Piscalat!</i>

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.020
It's way worse than that!

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:29.170
Nickel just lost in the blink of an eye!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:31.580
Right now, we don't stand a chance against—

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:36.090
Did you think I hadn't noticed you?

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:44.060
<i>Shit, shit, shit! 
What the hell do we do now?!</i>

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:47.870
S-So, Brandy... you wanna go next?

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:51.940
What— If Nickel got beat that easily,
 I won't win, either!

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:55.920
Aren't you always talking about 
how much stronger you are?!

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.980
I-I realize that, but...

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:00.780
I suppose you could say
that I was just being competitive...

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:00.780
We'll simply have to inform the Demon Lord...

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.190
<i>I suspect I'm looking at one the 
strongest cards the demons had to play.</i>

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.210
<i>Which means, as things currently stand...</i>

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:11.470
<i>Rin-san is unbeatable.</i>

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.420
Are you awake, Hayato?

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:18.840
Y-Yeah...

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:23.760
<i>But if they have power like this and 
and </i>haven't<i> taken over the world...</i>

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:27.850
<i>then they're just using the Zoble Empire
 as a means to stay hidden.</i>

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:31.850
<i>I see. Just like Prontea-san and myself.</i>

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:37.110
<i>Just the two of them, huh?</i>

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:41.400
<i>Intelligent demons, though...</i>

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:44.900
Come to think of it, there was mention of...

00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:48.330
Demon Lord Over-M, I think it was?

00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:50.710
Didn't Grandfather—

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:58.570
What's all the fuss?

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.510
Granny! We need to train right now!

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:05.360
I won't stand for an ass-kicking 
from anyone other than y—

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:06.550
Ooh!

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:13.230
You can take a nap until you 
finish regenerating, fool.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.950
Paula, where did Ysley skitter off to?

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:20.690
Oh, huh? Now that you 
mention it, I don't see him...

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:24.040
<i>Ysley-sama, we've recovered the monster</i>

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:26.030
and are ready to begin our study.

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:29.810
We're already analyzing the sample in detail.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:30.660
I see.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.100
Keep up the good work.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:36.910
I'll have another sample for you shortly.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:38.570
<i>The professor had budgetary—</i>

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:40.250
Money is no object this time around.

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:41.830
Spend however many billions you need.

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:45.070
You can arrange for additional 
facilities if need be.

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:47.720
But in exchange, I expect tangible results.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:49.720
Now, next is...

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.740
Hey there, Prontea-san!

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:54.730
Hey, Ysley-kun! It's been ages!

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.190
What have you been up to? 
Is Paula doing well?

00:20:57.190 --> 00:21:00.650
Does she still like to frolic in nature?

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:05.410
By the way, that Idaten theory you proposed 
has turned out to be incredible!

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.830
I can actually do things 
that seem like magic now.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.200
<i>I knew you could, Prontea-san.</i>

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.710
I'll be coming to see you soon.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:16.540
Maybe as soon as today.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:20.920
So Nickel was taken down 
without much struggle...

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:24.490
What shall we do now?
